      "postID": "58c6d550fd04b1785f747b88",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "What I have noticed is that IPD scaling effects sound in interesting ways, as it is currently.\n\nIt seems as if the scaling works from your viewpoint.  So a giant avatar, who can see things closer, yet smaller, can easily hear someone on the ground, where they can barely hear the giant, because technically they are far away like 15 or more feet away, but to the giant, the small person appears to be close only a few feet away, just small.\n\nIt's sort of the inverse of what you'd expect to hear.  A giant you'd think could be heard from far away, and small people you'd have to be close to hear\n\nI can see how that would be a problem, annoying to hear giants talking over everyone (even if it'd be more realistic.)\n\nHaving the option per-world to how volume Scaling is effected would be nice though",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
